  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a list of integers, find the first element that appears exactly once in the list.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains TTT - the number of test cases\nFor each test case:\n\nFirst line contains NNN - size of array\nSecond line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case print the first element that appears exactly once in the list\nIf no such element exists, print -1",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
